---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { steps } from '../data/steps';

const step = steps[0];
---

<GuideLayout step={step}>
  <h2>Introduction</h2>

  <p>
    Thailand has a growing tabletop community — locals, expats, and travelers who want a night of
    dice and story. Most pickup games organize on Facebook. English and Thai tables both exist;
    Chiang Mai and Bangkok are the densest hubs, but posts from other cities get replies too.
  </p>

  <p>
    You do not need a paid booking to play. This guide starts with free group finders, then covers
    in-person play at Game Tree Cafe in Chiang Mai, and ends with how to schedule a hosted seat if
    you want a table waiting for you.
  </p>

  <h2>What this guide covers</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Free Facebook groups to find players and DMs</li>
    <li>Playing in person at Game Tree Cafe (Chiang Mai)</li>
    <li>How to book an open session with a prepared GM</li>
  </ul>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Free groups first. Hosted games are optional — use them when you want less coordination and a
      seat ready on a known night.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>Who this is for</h2>

  <p>
    Beginners, tourists between flights, and regulars looking for a new table. If you already know a
    local group, great — if not, the next step is where most people start.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
